  "notes": "{自覚|じかく} means being conscious of one's own condition, situation, or responsibilities. Used as both a noun and a suru verb.\n\nWORD FORMATION:\n{自|じ} (self) + {覚|かく} (awareness, perception)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {自覚|じかく}がある: to be aware/conscious of\n- {自覚|じかく}する: to become aware, to realize\n- 〜の{自覚|じかく}を{持|も}つ: to have awareness of ~\n- {自覚|じかく}が{足|た}りない: to lack self-awareness\n\nMEDICAL USAGE:\n{自覚|じかく}{症状|しょうじょう} (subjective symptoms) refers to symptoms the patient can feel, as opposed to {他覚|たかく}{症状|しょうじょう} (objective symptoms found through examination).\n\nUSAGE:\nOften used when discussing responsibility or maturity: {社会人|しゃかいじん}としての{自覚|じかく} (awareness of being a working adult). Carries a nuance of moral or personal accountability.",
